POLICY EXCERPT (CARGO MARINE) — Policy No. CM-2024-8847

This is to certify that in consideration of the premium paid, the Underwriters agree to indemnify the Assured for loss or damage to the subject-matter insured, occurring during the period of insurance, in the manner and to the extent following:

INSURED PERILS: This insurance covers all risks of loss of or damage to the subject-matter insured, except as excluded. (All Risks per ICC(A))

EXCLUSIONS: This insurance excludes loss, damage, or expense caused by:
1. willful misconduct of the Assured;
2. ordinary leakage, ordinary loss in weight or volume, or ordinary wear and tear;
3. insufficiency or unsuitability of packing or preparation;
4. delay;
5. insolvency or financial default of owners, managers, charterers, or operators;
6. any weapon of war employing atomic or nuclear fission and/or fusion or other like reaction or radioactive force or matter.

Notwithstanding the above, this insurance covers loss of or damage to the subject-matter insured caused by fire, explosion, or collision, even if such fire, explosion, or collision is caused by a peril not otherwise covered. For the avoidance of doubt, fire or explosion following an act of war (whether war be declared or not) is covered hereunder.

PERIOD OF INSURANCE: From 2024-03-01 to 2025-02-28, both days inclusive, worldwide.

CLAIM DESCRIPTION (from call-centre agent notes):

Agent: 'Call from haulier re: container MAEU-1122334, voyage from Shanghai to Hamburg. Date of loss: 12/05/2024. Cargo: electronics in cartons. Vessel caught fire in engine room, fire spread to hold. Also reported explosion in adjacent container. Fire and explosion caused severe smoke and heat damage. Packing was standard export cartons. No info on willful misconduct. Policy number given: CM-2024-8847. Location: mid-ocean, within policy territory.'

